# L §5.5 Fan-out, L §8 (tally 2.1.8 R13, #169-k): a leg read as a field under an axis the walk reads fans out per
# combination, each with its own register. charge's leg is booked by a walk whose kasa balance reads pay, so under
# pa = lo the walk refuses it (kasa below zero) and the read is refused there; under pa = hi it is 10.00 DUK. Each
# tuple's line lists its own unfulfilled instance. 2.1.7's refcore printed one value with no head, or [pa = *] with
# the first combination's register.
=== m.tally
model pr
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-25
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "made up"

unit DUK: currency minor 0.01

axis pa
  lo "lower pay"
  hi "higher pay"

place kasa: claims DUK lives 2026-01-01..

place world: outside lives 2026-01-01..

input p_lo: money DUK

input p_hi: money DUK

input d1: date

input d2: date

input fee: money DUK

def pay: money DUK at d1
  rule base = p_lo
  rule hi beats base = p_hi when pa == hi

move salary: transfers
  on d1
  leg cash from world to kasa amount pay

move charge: transfers
  on d2
  leg cash from kasa to world amount fee

ask q_y: x.cash.amount for x in transfers over 2026-03-01 .. 2026-03-31

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  p_lo = 5.00
  p_hi = 20.00
  d1 = 2026-03-01
  d2 = 2026-03-02
  fee = 10.00
=== expect
q_y (x = salary) [pa = lo]: 5.00 DUK
  reading: pa = lo
  unfulfilled: salary
  cut 2026-10-25
q_y (x = salary) [pa = hi]: 20.00 DUK
  reading: pa = hi
  unfulfilled: salary
  cut 2026-10-25
q_y (x = charge) [pa = lo]: refused: RUN-PLACE kasa is -5.00 DUK after the day's observations and plans of 2026-03-02
  reading: pa = lo
  unfulfilled: charge
  cut 2026-10-25
q_y (x = charge) [pa = hi]: 10.00 DUK
  reading: pa = hi
  unfulfilled: charge
  cut 2026-10-25
